            <date type="death" when="1945"/>
            <note type="gender">M</note>
         </ab>
         <div type="bio">
            <p>Italian journalist from the Trieste area who spent the WWI years in <name type="person" key="G_CHE_ZURI">Zurich</name>. During that time he had an office at Bahnhofplatz and was a correspondent for a newspaper in Turin. When JJ was suffering from vision problems in February and March 1917, he dictated several letters to Battara. Battara drew on his wartime experience in Switzerland to write <name type="work">La Svizzera d'ieri e d'oggi</name> (Milan: R. Caddeo, 1921). <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
